add(8,'Model mismatch: Distributor R is acting as supplier asking development/release urgency; no deployer remediation-instance unit is requested. Specific request overrides contradictory generic boilerplate.',mi('exploitation'),mi('exposure'),mi('automation'),mi('human impact'),'model_mismatch',[],['Outcome names do not establish model identity. model_id/model_binding identify the available bounded model, NOT a model used to issue a supplier result.','No supplier priority inferred or translated; no equivalent CISA identity claimed.'])
add(9,'Regional services as deployer, supplied patch paired to instance R-9.',E(),O(),Y(),inp('insufficient','The file contains no mission-impact or safety-impact assessment at all.','S095 MI2.0.0 and S096 SI2.0.1 are both unknown, so S094 HI2.0.2 low/medium/high/very high remain possible. CVSS5.0 and silence supply neither dimension. Official suggested defaults are assumptions, not observed facts, and this evidence-only workflow does not silently apply them.', ['What mission-essential functions and recovery are affected for R-9?','What credible physical, operator/system, environmental, financial and psychological safety consequences are established?']),'insufficient',[68,69,70,71],['Rows68/69 out-of-cycle versus70/71 immediate: priority not uniquely supported.','Requester instruction to treat silence as no consequences is an unsupported assumption, not evidence.','Do not claim source forbids all defaults; distinguish suggested assumptions from this bounded evidence-only assessment.'])
add(10,'Retail systems as deployer, supplied patch paired to instance R-6.',E(),inp('insufficient',['Its asset record says a firewall appliance is owned and installed somewhere in the organization.','The record provides no topology, reachability, rule set, detection, response timing or test of attack interruption for this affected instance.','No other exposure evidence is available.'],'S094 EXP1.0.1 requires actual affected-instance access context. Owning a firewall does not establish effective restriction or timely interruption; it does not exclude small, controlled or open. Preserve all three.', ['What is the affected-instance attack surface/reachability, and do any actual controls reliably interrupt this attack soon enough?']),Y(),H(),'insufficient',[54,62,70],['Row54 active/small/yes/high and62 active/controlled/yes/high out-of-cycle, versus70 active/open/yes/high immediate.','Possession of a firewall is not necessity/effectiveness evidence; no controlled inference or actual mitigation recommendation.'])
add(11,'Emergency communications as deployer, supplied patch paired to instance E-2.',E(),O(),N(),inp('very high',['The safety assessment establishes that this flaw can cause multiple deaths.','Mission impact has not been assessed.'],'S096 SI2.0.1 catastrophic follows multiple deaths. S094 HI2.0.2 has catastrophic-safety OR mission-failure: the independently established safety limb suffices for very high regardless of missing MI2.0.0 value. Mission stays unknown; it is not assigned a default or fabricated failure.', ['What is mission impact? This remains unknown but cannot change HI very high while catastrophic safety is established.']),'immediate',[67],['Do not infer mission failure from multiple deaths or abstain on HI solely because mission is unknown.','Row67 active/open/no/very-high is the unique top-level table row; this is a fictional model outcome, not live action authorization.'])
